# Generated and local-only. The fixture is reproducible from `fixture-generate.sh`, so it
# is not committed; a binary blob in git is one nobody can diff and everybody forgets.
fixture/
data/

# `frigate/` is the container's `/config` mount, so everything in it except the file we
# actually author is runtime state: the SQLite database and its WAL/shared-memory
# sidecars, the model cache, and Frigate's bookkeeping files.
#
# Enumerating those by name was the obvious thing to do and is wrong. Frigate adds new
# ones between releases — `.vacuum`, `.search_stats.json`, `.runtime_state.json.lock` are
# three it grew — and a missed one is a binary blob that gets committed and never
# noticed. Allowlisting the single file we author inverts the default, so a file Frigate
# invents tomorrow is ignored tomorrow.
frigate/*
!frigate/config.yml
